@title Should we move to a monorepo?
@subtitle Proposal for the web platform group
@author Kenji Watanabe
@date 2026-09-30

We have 23 repositories for one product. A change to the design system takes, on average, four pull requests and two days of version bumps before it reaches the checkout page.

## Pros

- One pull request for a cross-cutting change
- Shared lint, test and build configuration
- Atomic refactors across packages
- Easier onboarding: one clone, one README

## Cons

- CI must learn to build only what changed
- Repository permissions get coarser
- A one-time migration of about three weeks
- Git operations slow down past a few million files

## Recommendation

! **Migrate in Q1**, starting with the design system and the two apps that consume it. Keep the payments service separate until its audit finishes.
